cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "XrayAttenuation.jl: NIST XCOM photon attenuation coefficients with K-edge aware interpolation"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Dale
    family-names: Black
    affiliation: "University of California, Irvine — Molloi Lab"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9150-9827"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Dale-Black/XrayAttenuation.jl"
url: "https://github.com/Dale-Black/XrayAttenuation.jl"
abstract: >-
  Julia package providing X-ray photon attenuation coefficients from
  the NIST XCOM database for all 92 elements, a curated catalog of
  100+ predefined materials (tissues, bones, polymers, detectors,
  contrast agents, Gammex 472 CT calibration inserts), and compound /
  mixture composition by chemical formula or mass fraction. Uses
  K-edge-aware interpolation for accurate cross-sections near
  absorption edges and integrates with Unitful.jl for dimensionally
  correct queries.
keywords:
  - X-ray
  - photon attenuation
  - NIST XCOM
  - computed tomography
  - dual-energy CT
  - K-edge
  - Julia
  - scientific computing
license: MIT
version: "0.3.1"
